        {
          "id": 1341128976,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, the generic term \"plugin\" would cover extcap.  \n  \nBut Wireshark terminology for \"plugin\" covers a specific list ([README.plugins](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/doc/README.plugins)):  \n> Currently plugin APIs are available for dissectors (epan), capture file types\n(wiretap) and media decoders (codecs).  \n  \nIf `extcap` are plugins, they should they be in `C:\\Program Files\\Wireshark\\plugins` instead of `C:\\Program Files\\Wireshark\\extcap`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
